WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.148
What?

3
00:02:34.029 --> 00:02:35.864
I can't understand.

4
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.460
Speak plainly.

5
00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:53.964
{\an8}YOU CREATED ME. DAEMON.

6
00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.049
{\an8}Stop.

7
00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.091
{\an8}YET YOU ARE NOW SET
ON DESTROYING ME.

8
00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:57.177
{\an8}Stop it.

9
00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:03.350
{\an8}ALL BECAUSE YOUR BROTHER
LOVED ME MORE THAN HE DID YOU.

10
00:03:16.071 --> 00:03:18.990
{\an8}THIS IS WHAT YOU ALWAYS
WANTED. IS IT NOT?

11
00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:30.627
There's been a raven.

12
00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:37.592
Good morrow. Your Grace.

13
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.221
Slept well. I trust?

14
00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.140
As I said. there's been a raven.

15
00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.895
Aegon's army departed King's
Landing a fortnight ago.

16
00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:54.775
The castles of Rosby and Stokeworth
have both fallen without siege.

17
00:03:54.776 --> 00:03:57.152
They have raised Aegon's banner

18
00:03:57.153 --> 00:04:00.657
and added their levies to
Ser Criston Cole's host.

19
00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:04.243
Both houses cited that

20
00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.914
sad business with the usurper's
son in their declarations.

21
00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.583
Ser Criston's army.

22
00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:16.588
now tripled in strength. might
have Harrenhal as its destination.

23
00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.967
Even if you can raise
a host of Rivermen.

24
00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:23.013
they will not be ready
in time to face him.

25
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:32.063
Let's see what your Lord
Paramount is made of.

26
00:04:37.736 --> 00:04:40.946
My prince... My Grace.

27
00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.449
Your Grace.

28
00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:46.410
Lord Grover is looking more hale
and healthy than I expected.

29
00:04:46.411 --> 00:04:49.204
This is Ser Oscar Tully.
grandson to Grover Tully.

30
00:04:49.205 --> 00:04:50.873
He is heir to Riverrun

31
00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:54.001
and the future Lord
Paramount of the Riverlands.

32
00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:57.546
His Grace. the King
Consort. Daemon Targaryen.

33
00:04:57.547 --> 00:05:00.300
- It is an honor. Your Grace.
- Indeed.

34
00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:08.808
How fares your grandsire?

35
00:05:12.771 --> 00:05:16.023
Sadly. he remains incapacitated.

36
00:05:16.024 --> 00:05:18.734
He lies in a kind
of waking sleep.

37
00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:22.279
unable to do much more
than take meager drink.

38
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.240
It is barely enough
to sustain him.

39
00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:26.700
So. he's alive?

40
00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:29.119
Yes. gods be good.

41
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.872
Well. my time is short and
I have need of an army.

42
00:05:31.873 --> 00:05:34.166
Perhaps you might place a
feather pillow over his head

43
00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.503
and speed along
your inheritance?

44
00:05:38.588 --> 00:05:42.258
I love my grandsire.
like a father.

45
00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:46.596
My own lord father died
suddenly. himself a young man.

46
00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:49.848
Lord Grover raised
me in his stead.

47
00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.225
All very touching.

48
00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:53.227
Are you here to speak with
your grandsire's voice?

49
00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:55.229
For House Tully
and the Riverlands?

50
00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.815
While he still lives?

51
00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:02.987
- That is not our way.
- Then you're of no use to me.

52
00:06:03.947 --> 00:06:05.656
I can see why the
Blackwoods and the Brackens

53
00:06:05.657 --> 00:06:09.368
did not fear to start a war beneath
the nose of their liege lords.

54
00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.662
House Tully is a
fish with no head.

55
00:06:11.663 --> 00:06:15.666
Remind me which of your countrymen
claim to fight in the name of Aegon?

56
00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:17.876
Was it Bracken or Blackwood?

57
00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.587
It was House Bracken that
declared Green. Your Grace.

58
00:06:20.588 --> 00:06:21.881
Who could remember.

59
00:06:23.008 --> 00:06:24.008
Summon the Blackwoods here.

60
00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:27.178
I require men of action to
lead my host of Rivermen.

61
00:06:56.041 --> 00:06:57.459
M'lady.

62
00:07:01.004 --> 00:07:04.673
"Princess." if we're
holding to formalities.

63
00:07:04.674 --> 00:07:07.385
Apologies. Princess.

64
00:07:08.762 --> 00:07:10.680
And you are Alyn.

65
00:07:11.222 --> 00:07:13.433
Yes. Princess.

66
00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:18.313
I'm given to understand my
lord husband owes you his life.

67
00:07:21.483 --> 00:07:24.527
But I was not told his
savior was so comely.

68
00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:28.322
Your mother must've
been very beautiful.

69
00:07:28.323 --> 00:07:29.532
Rhaenys.

70
00:07:38.166 --> 00:07:40.418
- Is your work finished?
- No. m'lord.

71
00:07:51.721 --> 00:07:53.765
I just had a word
with your captains.

72
00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:59.145
He was the sailor who plucked
you from your watery grave?

73
00:08:06.861 --> 00:08:07.862
Yes.

74
00:08:09.364 --> 00:08:11.032
You did not think to mention it?

75
00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:13.660
I did not think it relevant.

76
00:08:16.037 --> 00:08:18.039
I know who he is. Corlys.

77
00:08:20.417 --> 00:08:23.336
Alyn's past is no fault of his.

78
00:08:24.087 --> 00:08:25.129
He saved his lord's life.

79
00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:27.673
He should be raised up and honored.
not hidden beneath the tides.

80
00:08:27.674 --> 00:08:29.759
Is this why you came?

81
00:08:30.885 --> 00:08:32.554
To subject me to an inquisition?

82
00:08:34.806 --> 00:08:38.600
I came to tell you that Baela
has called me to Dragonstone.

83
00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:39.936
Baela?

84
00:08:41.062 --> 00:08:43.647
That council is going to dine
on her and Jace for supper.

85
00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:45.774
They grow restless in
Rhaenyra's absence.

86
00:08:45.775 --> 00:08:49.236
Still. where has
that woman gone?

87
00:08:49.237 --> 00:08:52.407
I suspect to try and draw
us all back from the abyss.

88
00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:18.224
- Good morrow. Your Grace.
- Good morrow. Grand Maester.

89
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.646
As requested.

90
00:09:24.647 --> 00:09:27.275
- I brewed it myself.
- Thank you.

91
00:09:28.276 --> 00:09:30.278
I will see it
delivered discreetly.

92
00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:35.949
Do report if the recipient
has need of any remedy.

93
00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.370
The tea is known to
disagree with the gut.

94
00:09:39.204 --> 00:09:41.331
I shall observe
the girl closely.

95
00:09:47.962 --> 00:09:49.589
Grand Maester.

96
00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:59.974
You've ever been a practical man.
an honorable servant to the crown.

97
00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.770
And you served my lord
husband in his darkest hours.

98
00:10:04.938 --> 00:10:06.773
Such was my duty. Your Grace.

99
00:10:08.566 --> 00:10:09.776
Tell me.

100
00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:15.073
Do you believe Viserys
wanted Aegon to succeed him?

101
00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.830
I could not know.

102
00:10:23.748 --> 00:10:26.751
His Grace never raised
the matter with me.

103
00:11:26.353 --> 00:11:29.355
Ser Criston Cole's host has taken
to exploiting the tree cover

104
00:11:29.356 --> 00:11:30.647
to conceal its movements.

105
00:11:30.648 --> 00:11:33.650
He now only travels by night
to confound our dragons.

106
00:11:33.651 --> 00:11:35.611
And what is Cole's heading?

107
00:11:35.612 --> 00:11:37.154
It is difficult to say.
but there were signs

108
00:11:37.155 --> 00:11:40.240
of an army moving
northwest. I believe.

109
00:11:40.241 --> 00:11:41.700
She believes.

110
00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:43.786
You should've burned them
when you had the chance.

111
00:11:43.787 --> 00:11:46.539
Perhaps you can. Ser Alfred. when
you next sight them on your dragon.

112
00:11:47.791 --> 00:11:51.543
The only reason we know any of
this is because of Baela's efforts.

113
00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:53.212
What do we know. my prince?

114
00:11:53.213 --> 00:11:55.589
If you ask me. it
is little and less.

115
00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:58.342
We know that Cole possesses a
host that is growing in strength

116
00:11:58.343 --> 00:11:59.635
and that it is a problem.

117
00:11:59.636 --> 00:12:02.554
Can Daemon hope to meet
it with his own in time?

118
00:12:02.555 --> 00:12:03.847
And if I know the Riverlands.

119
00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:09.061
he has more disentangling ahead of
him than the end of a Lyseni orgy.

120
00:12:09.062 --> 00:12:12.607
Have you heard word
from your father?

121
00:12:15.151 --> 00:12:18.654
- No.
- Ravens were sent to Harrenhal

122
00:12:18.655 --> 00:12:21.824
seeking news of Daemon's
progress with the Riverlords.

123
00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:24.284
None have. as yet. returned.

124
00:12:24.285 --> 00:12:25.453
Just so.

125
00:12:25.995 --> 00:12:28.372
An enemy host. growing
in constitution.

126
00:12:28.373 --> 00:12:33.252
marches somewhere in the
vastness of the Crownlands.

127
00:12:33.253 --> 00:12:36.922
We could. perhaps. act if
only we had a host of our own.

128
00:12:36.923 --> 00:12:38.299
Or someone here to lead us.

129
00:12:39.009 --> 00:12:40.885
Mind your tongue. Ser Alfred.

130
00:12:42.387 --> 00:12:44.763
Does it speak
falsely. my prince?

131
00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:47.224
This council is rudderless.

132
00:12:47.225 --> 00:12:49.561
I'm doing my best to
steer it. Ser Alfred.

133
00:12:51.146 --> 00:12:54.773
Why should your voice be any
louder than ours. Princess?

134
00:12:54.774 --> 00:12:56.692
The queen did not name you Hand.

135
00:12:56.693 --> 00:12:59.153
It is her voice. and
that of the king consort.

136
00:12:59.154 --> 00:13:02.448
that we need to raise alliances
and command our vassals.

137
00:13:02.449 --> 00:13:05.410
- But they are gone.
- What has come of this council?

138
00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.208
My lord.

139
00:13:15.211 --> 00:13:18.589
Our enemy is on the march.

140
00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:20.716
Is there naught to be done
in the absence of the queen

141
00:13:20.717 --> 00:13:24.054
but to grouse and
claw for power?

142
00:13:30.185 --> 00:13:32.604
We do not know the
queen's doings.

143
00:13:33.772 --> 00:13:38.360
But we must trust that she seeks the
same as each of us at this table.

144
00:13:39.986 --> 00:13:42.405
An end to this conflict.

145
00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.720
Men of House Darklyn.

146
00:14:06.721 --> 00:14:10.809
All who bend the knee to the
true king. Aegon. will be spared.

147
00:14:11.976 --> 00:14:14.561
You can earn back your
honor by raising his banner

148
00:14:14.562 --> 00:14:19.150
and fighting in his name against
the Whore of Dragonstone.

149
00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.112
All who refuse.

150
00:14:23.571 --> 00:14:25.573
will have their death.

151
00:14:39.629 --> 00:14:41.172
Good morrow. Lord Darklyn.

152
00:14:42.007 --> 00:14:45.426
Is there no honor left
in this world. Cole?

153
00:14:45.427 --> 00:14:50.264
Sacking your queen's own castles
and putting her people to the sword?

154
00:14:50.265 --> 00:14:51.975
"Kingmaker."

155
00:14:56.312 --> 00:14:58.648
You are not fit for
the white cloak.

156
00:15:02.235 --> 00:15:05.238
This is a better death
than a traitor deserves.

157
00:15:05.739 --> 00:15:07.866
You should thank me for it.

158
00:15:10.076 --> 00:15:12.328
Yours will come in kind.

159
00:15:27.635 --> 00:15:28.845
Lord Hand.

160
00:15:44.319 --> 00:15:47.947
We'll lead the van northeast.
follow the coastline.

161
00:15:49.491 --> 00:15:51.075
I realize you were
neither born nor bred

162
00:15:51.076 --> 00:15:54.453
anywhere near the Crownlands.
my good Lord Hand.

163
00:15:54.454 --> 00:15:56.956
but Harrenhal is to the west.

164
00:16:01.002 --> 00:16:02.545
Indeed it is.

165
00:16:05.507 --> 00:16:08.676
Fuck you. I told you we
should've sent our dragons.

166
00:16:08.677 --> 00:16:10.595
And now look what's happened.

167
00:16:11.012 --> 00:16:13.764
Daemon. of all people.
has taken Harrenhal.

168
00:16:13.765 --> 00:16:16.266
I give you a job. and
now you just sit there.

169
00:16:16.267 --> 00:16:18.770
It's your fucking castle!

170
00:16:20.522 --> 00:16:24.484
Well. that castle is more
crippled than I am. Your Grace.

171
00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:28.654
It's like to drive Daemon to madness
as he attempts to make use of it.

172
00:16:28.655 --> 00:16:30.990
It is beyond his faculties.

173
00:16:31.866 --> 00:16:35.828
It is also penniless. as I
happily control all of its gold.

174
00:16:35.829 --> 00:16:39.456
So. as Harrenhal saps
Daemon's resolve.

175
00:16:39.457 --> 00:16:41.917
the false queen remains
trapped on her island.

176
00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:45.255
and Ser Criston continues felling
castles in the Crownlands.

177
00:16:47.799 --> 00:16:52.136
I need to be informed of these things
if I am to make informed rulings.

178
00:16:52.137 --> 00:16:54.054
I will not be made to
look a fool in front of

179
00:16:54.055 --> 00:16:56.725
- my allies and enemies.
- Harrenhal must wait.

180
00:17:00.353 --> 00:17:02.689
Ser Criston is marching
on Rook's Rest.

181
00:17:03.565 --> 00:17:05.274
Rook's Re... A pathetic prize.

182
00:17:05.275 --> 00:17:07.402
- I gave no such command...
- The castle is small.

183
00:17:08.653 --> 00:17:09.903
weakly defended.

184
00:17:09.904 --> 00:17:13.032
and Lord Staunton sits
on Rhaenyra's council.

185
00:17:13.033 --> 00:17:15.242
After Cole smashes it.

186
00:17:15.243 --> 00:17:17.579
we'll have Dragonstone
effectively cut off by land.

187
00:17:19.372 --> 00:17:22.082
This war will not be
won with dragons alone

188
00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:25.210
but with dragons flying
behind armies of men.

189
00:17:25.211 --> 00:17:29.132
No! Have him turn about.
I want Harrenhal back.

190
00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.510
Cole is already
preparing his attack.

191
00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.929
How do you know this?

192
00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:38.016
He sent word to me.

193
00:17:38.975 --> 00:17:40.185
To you?

194
00:17:42.979 --> 00:17:45.190
The two of you have been

195
00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:49.569
plotting without my authority?

196
00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:57.327
{\an8}YOU HAD MORE PRESSING
MATTERS TO ATTEND TO.

197
00:17:58.036 --> 00:18:03.375
{\an8}SUCH AS HOLDING COURT.
CHOOSING YOUR SOBRIQUET.

198
00:18:03.917 --> 00:18:07.337
{\an8}AND NAMING IMBECILIC
LICKSPITTLES TO OUR KINGSGUARD.

199
00:18:11.925 --> 00:18:15.303
{\an8}DO YOU HAVE A WISER
STRATEGY. MY KING?

200
00:18:17.222 --> 00:18:21.518
{\an8}IF SO. YOU SHOULD VOICE
IT TO YOUR COUNCIL.

201
00:18:22.852 --> 00:18:25.689
{\an8}WE ALL AWAIT YOUR ANSWER.

202
00:18:34.948 --> 00:18:37.242
{\an8}I CAN HAVE TO...

203
00:18:38.702 --> 00:18:40.870
{\an8}MAKE A...

204
00:18:41.538 --> 00:18:42.872
{\an8}WAR?

205
00:18:52.424 --> 00:18:54.717
Harrenhal is a useful morass.

206
00:18:54.718 --> 00:18:57.678
It will keep Daemon well-occupied
while we strengthen our host

207
00:18:57.679 --> 00:18:59.930
and weaken Rhaenyra's
support on the mainland.

208
00:18:59.931 --> 00:19:02.975
We will deal with it in
the Riverlands in time.

209
00:19:02.976 --> 00:19:07.354
But right now. Rook's
Rest is an easy target

210
00:19:07.355 --> 00:19:09.357
and a worthy effort.

211
00:19:10.483 --> 00:19:13.445
Don't you agree. my king?

212
00:19:28.418 --> 00:19:29.711
Come.

213
00:19:33.882 --> 00:19:35.508
Lord Larys.

214
00:19:39.346 --> 00:19:44.308
I thought I'd look in on you. Your Grace.
after your absence from the small council.

215
00:19:44.309 --> 00:19:46.353
I feared something was amiss.

216
00:19:47.479 --> 00:19:52.024
You're kind to do so. my lord.
but indulgence was my sin.

217
00:19:52.025 --> 00:19:55.277
I ventured into the lamprey
pie at last night's supper.

218
00:19:55.278 --> 00:19:57.197
Too far. I fear.

219
00:20:03.703 --> 00:20:06.122
That is a rich indulgence.

220
00:20:06.998 --> 00:20:10.584
But I believe it is a sin
to deny your appetites.

221
00:20:10.585 --> 00:20:13.880
They are what make us
fully alive as mortal men.

222
00:20:18.176 --> 00:20:20.552
Was anything of note
discussed at the council?

223
00:20:20.553 --> 00:20:25.391
Daemon having seized Harrenhal and
His Grace's resulting displeasure.

224
00:20:25.392 --> 00:20:29.270
I would've thought you would
be the most aggrieved. my lord.

225
00:20:30.397 --> 00:20:32.607
I see it as a loss
for our greater good.

226
00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:36.527
Dragonstone's attentions
are greatly divided.

227
00:20:36.528 --> 00:20:39.781
First in the Riverlands and the
Gullet. and now the Crownlands.

228
00:20:40.782 --> 00:20:42.658
Ser Criston wins every
challenge he faces there.

229
00:20:42.659 --> 00:20:46.162
That truth alone is like
to incite Rhaenyra's fury.

230
00:20:46.913 --> 00:20:49.541
He's covered himself
in glory. to be sure.

231
00:20:50.667 --> 00:20:53.128
And you must worry for him?

232
00:20:53.628 --> 00:20:55.839
Your sworn sword.

233
00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:59.758
on the march. ever
exposed to dragons?

234
00:20:59.759 --> 00:21:01.803
It is a perilous road.

235
00:21:05.223 --> 00:21:07.225
Ser Criston is the
Hand of the King.

236
00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:11.187
We should all pray for his
victory and safe return.

237
00:21:12.272 --> 00:21:13.481
Indeed.

238
00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:26.870
If I may be so bold. my queen.

239
00:21:32.584 --> 00:21:35.003
you have not seemed
yourself of late.

240
00:21:36.546 --> 00:21:38.839
Only weeks ago. my
lord husband was alive

241
00:21:38.840 --> 00:21:40.925
and the realm was at peace.

242
00:21:41.384 --> 00:21:46.180
Now. I've barely had the hours to grieve
one tragedy before suffering the next.

243
00:21:46.181 --> 00:21:49.142
I regret if I have
not been myself.

244
00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:56.107
I did not know you shared
your lord husband's love

245
00:21:57.192 --> 00:21:59.027
for the histories.

246
00:22:00.445 --> 00:22:03.365
If not his love. then
certainly an abiding interest.

247
00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:06.909
The voices of history
guided Viserys.

248
00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:10.038
He knew that his wisdom alone
could only reach so far.

249
00:22:10.413 --> 00:22:12.916
Do you think that is
why he changed his mind

250
00:22:14.292 --> 00:22:15.710
in the end?

251
00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:20.798
No matter how suited he
thought Rhaenyra for the crown.

252
00:22:20.799 --> 00:22:25.427
the voices of
history. as you say.

253
00:22:25.428 --> 00:22:29.139
would have told him how the realm
would react to her succession.

254
00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:30.766
It was impossible to know
what steered his thoughts

255
00:22:30.767 --> 00:22:32.686
in those final hours.

256
00:22:33.937 --> 00:22:36.147
Do you now doubt his intentions?

257
00:22:43.863 --> 00:22:46.491
Rhaenyra's supporters will
believe what they wish.

258
00:22:47.117 --> 00:22:49.119
And so will Aegon's.

259
00:22:49.953 --> 00:22:53.248
The war will be
fought. many will die

260
00:22:54.499 --> 00:22:57.127
and the victor will
eventually ascend the throne.

261
00:22:59.045 --> 00:23:02.048
The significance of Viserys's
intentions died with him.

262
00:23:08.805 --> 00:23:10.265
Yes. it did.

263
00:24:47.737 --> 00:24:50.322
It's a touch late to be
stalkin' about a strange castle.

264
00:24:50.323 --> 00:24:52.449
putting its people to the sword.

265
00:24:52.450 --> 00:24:53.743
You.

266
00:24:54.953 --> 00:24:56.788
I'm called Alys.

267
00:24:57.372 --> 00:24:58.789
Strong?

268
00:24:58.790 --> 00:25:00.041
Rivers.

269
00:25:01.084 --> 00:25:02.293
A bastard.

270
00:25:02.836 --> 00:25:05.463
Once you get to know me.
you'll find I'm not so bad.

271
00:25:06.214 --> 00:25:08.674
So what are you then?
Some kind of maester?

272
00:25:08.675 --> 00:25:10.634
In a manner of speaking.

273
00:25:10.635 --> 00:25:14.304
I inherited the duties after
the last one fled in the night.

274
00:25:14.305 --> 00:25:17.308
- Fled? Why?
- Just never settled in.

275
00:25:20.061 --> 00:25:22.063
How are you settling in?

276
00:25:22.731 --> 00:25:25.900
I've come to know the face
of tortured rest well enough.

277
00:25:26.526 --> 00:25:29.529
Sleep can be thin in this place.

278
00:25:31.114 --> 00:25:33.033
What would you know of my sleep?

279
00:25:34.159 --> 00:25:37.412
Harrenhal's been cursed since
its first stone was laid.

280
00:25:38.496 --> 00:25:40.873
Black Harren felled the
grove of weirwood trees

281
00:25:40.874 --> 00:25:43.083
that grew on these lands.

282
00:25:43.084 --> 00:25:47.421
Heart trees. imbued with the spirits
of those who lived long before he came.

283
00:25:47.422 --> 00:25:49.673
It's said their whispers can
still be heard sometimes.

284
00:25:49.674 --> 00:25:51.175
A midwife's tale.

285
00:25:51.176 --> 00:25:54.888
The very bed you sleep in was
made from such a heart tree.

286
00:25:56.598 --> 00:26:00.143
Have you experienced
anything of note?

287
00:26:00.810 --> 00:26:03.229
You are a strange kind of woman.

288
00:26:03.688 --> 00:26:05.857
I'm no woman at
all. I'm a barn owl.

289
00:26:06.441 --> 00:26:08.443
Cursed to live in human form.

290
00:26:11.321 --> 00:26:13.361
So you've come here after
quarreling with your wife?

291
00:26:14.324 --> 00:26:15.408
What?

292
00:26:16.743 --> 00:26:21.623
You arrive here alone to claim the
castle and yet. send no ravens.

293
00:26:23.833 --> 00:26:26.503
Do you now plan to
make your own claim?

294
00:26:27.003 --> 00:26:29.171
- Perhaps to prove yourself to her.
- Do not try me

295
00:26:29.172 --> 00:26:31.131
with your insolence. witch.

296
00:26:31.132 --> 00:26:35.887
It's a hard thing. I imagine. to give
obeisance to one who replaced you as heir.

297
00:26:39.099 --> 00:26:40.433
And a woman too. A...

298
00:26:41.393 --> 00:26:44.020
girl child you
bounced on your knee.

299
00:26:46.398 --> 00:26:49.108
Does it please you that her
legitimacy is contested?

300
00:26:49.109 --> 00:26:53.071
As you stand here. with
a castle and a dragon

301
00:26:53.905 --> 00:26:56.116
attempting to draw
an army of men.

302
00:27:01.204 --> 00:27:02.831
Here. Drink this.

303
00:27:04.749 --> 00:27:08.378
You'll need your sleep if you're
to win this place to your side.

304
00:27:17.887 --> 00:27:21.349
I now rule my house as regent until
my nephew Benjicot comes of age.

305
00:27:26.730 --> 00:27:29.732
The Brackens are venal cravens

306
00:27:29.733 --> 00:27:32.944
and they must pay for their treachery
against the laws of gods and men.

307
00:27:34.612 --> 00:27:36.281
And against the crown.

308
00:27:36.698 --> 00:27:38.157
Who are you?

309
00:27:38.158 --> 00:27:39.825
Ser Willem Blackwood
of House Blackwood.

310
00:27:39.826 --> 00:27:42.454
Your Grace. as I said.

311
00:27:46.750 --> 00:27:47.959
Well met.

312
00:27:49.002 --> 00:27:50.794
What might I do for you?

313
00:27:50.795 --> 00:27:54.049
It was you who summoned
me. Your Grace.

314
00:27:55.133 --> 00:27:58.135
I was given to understand
that you wanted an army.

315
00:27:58.136 --> 00:27:59.928
Well. who doesn't these days?

316
00:27:59.929 --> 00:28:01.805
You Blackwoods certainly
never miss a chance

317
00:28:01.806 --> 00:28:04.893
to bloody your swords. do you?

318
00:28:05.935 --> 00:28:09.271
Some 20 years ago. my lord
bent the knee to King Viserys

319
00:28:09.272 --> 00:28:12.649
and acknowledged the Princess
Rhaenyra as his rightful heir.

320
00:28:12.650 --> 00:28:14.443
So you fight for this old oath?

321
00:28:14.444 --> 00:28:17.489
Not. of course. for your
thousand-year-old feud with the Brackens.

322
00:28:19.199 --> 00:28:21.618
I once vied for
Queen Rhaenyra's hand

323
00:28:22.327 --> 00:28:24.162
before she wed Ser Laenor.

324
00:28:24.829 --> 00:28:26.956
I always liked her spirit.

325
00:28:27.540 --> 00:28:29.416
She had the true
blood of the dragon.

326
00:28:29.417 --> 00:28:33.088
And you're prepared to march
without the leave of your lord...

327
00:28:55.777 --> 00:28:57.028
Your Grace?

328
00:28:58.947 --> 00:29:00.656
And once you and your dragon

329
00:29:00.657 --> 00:29:03.827
bring the queen's
justice to the Brackens

330
00:29:04.285 --> 00:29:06.287
our armies will be yours.

331
00:29:15.505 --> 00:29:18.090
Our lords in the
Crownlands are grousing.

332
00:29:18.091 --> 00:29:20.050
Their herds of livestock
struggle to keep pace

333
00:29:20.051 --> 00:29:21.844
with the dragons'
relentless appetites.

334
00:29:21.845 --> 00:29:24.263
- Vhagar's in particular.
- They can either provide

335
00:29:24.264 --> 00:29:27.433
the crown what it needs. or
we can claim their holdings.

336
00:29:27.434 --> 00:29:28.976
Oh. that would be a relief.

337
00:29:28.977 --> 00:29:31.478
as we have no more coin
to lend to the effort.

338
00:29:31.479 --> 00:29:34.148
Resources are certainly
growing no more plentiful

339
00:29:34.149 --> 00:29:35.274
in the face of the blockade.

340
00:29:35.275 --> 00:29:37.609
The demand on the blacksmiths.
armorers and tanners for equipment

341
00:29:37.610 --> 00:29:39.987
has only grown apace
with Ser Criston's army.

342
00:29:39.988 --> 00:29:42.031
Well. Cole's done
splendidly. at the least.

343
00:29:42.032 --> 00:29:45.910
turning every castle and army he's faced.
including Duskendale. gods bless him.

344
00:29:47.162 --> 00:29:49.121
The Kingmaker.
they're calling him.

345
00:29:49.122 --> 00:29:51.415
And with Aemond and
Vhagar also at the ready.

346
00:29:51.416 --> 00:29:53.626
we are a formidable opponent.

347
00:29:54.919 --> 00:29:56.629
You bore me.

348
00:29:59.466 --> 00:30:01.468
You all bore me.

349
00:30:17.525 --> 00:30:20.027
Perhaps Ser Criston
will be able to procure

350
00:30:20.028 --> 00:30:22.029
more livestock
through his campaign.

351
00:30:22.030 --> 00:30:24.783
Any coin we can save
will be a welcome bounty.

352
00:30:34.793 --> 00:30:36.168
What are you doing here?

353
00:30:36.169 --> 00:30:37.795
Where are your father's books?

354
00:30:37.796 --> 00:30:39.005
I ordered them removed.

355
00:30:39.798 --> 00:30:42.592
With no thought to the centuries
of knowledge in those pages.

356
00:30:49.349 --> 00:30:50.975
Your Grace.

357
00:30:52.519 --> 00:30:55.188
I removed them. I
didn't burn them.

358
00:31:00.402 --> 00:31:01.777
What is it?

359
00:31:01.778 --> 00:31:04.114
They don't care what I think.

360
00:31:06.783 --> 00:31:09.076
- Who. Aegon?
- My council.

361
00:31:09.077 --> 00:31:11.245
Cole. Aemond. They
pursue their campaign

362
00:31:11.246 --> 00:31:13.415
without seeking my aid.
or even my thoughts.

363
00:31:16.710 --> 00:31:18.169
What thoughts would you have?

364
00:31:19.629 --> 00:31:21.506
I'm the king.

365
00:31:24.968 --> 00:31:27.804
Do you think simply wearing the
crown imbues you with wisdom?

366
00:31:34.519 --> 00:31:37.939
Those men at your council table

367
00:31:38.898 --> 00:31:40.900
earned their seats.

368
00:31:41.401 --> 00:31:44.695
It was my hope that
once enthroned.

369
00:31:44.696 --> 00:31:47.072
you would honor the
burden of your new duties.

370
00:31:47.073 --> 00:31:49.033
be silent.

371
00:31:49.034 --> 00:31:52.746
and strive to learn from the
more studied minds around you.

372
00:31:54.247 --> 00:31:57.250
In the hope that you might be
half the king your father was.

373
00:31:58.877 --> 00:32:00.879
- Tread carefully.
- Or what?

374
00:32:03.006 --> 00:32:06.050
You'll hang me. as you
did your ratcatchers?

375
00:32:06.051 --> 00:32:08.511
Or have me banished.
as you did your Hand?

376
00:32:10.180 --> 00:32:11.555
I ruled

377
00:32:11.556 --> 00:32:13.974
in your father's absence
throughout his long illness.

378
00:32:13.975 --> 00:32:16.643
and Otto Hightower was as cunning
a statesman as ever lived.

379
00:32:16.644 --> 00:32:21.941
You should humbly be seeking
our opinions and counsel.

380
00:32:24.277 --> 00:32:26.236
You have no idea the
sacrifices that were made

381
00:32:26.237 --> 00:32:28.531
to put you on that throne.

382
00:32:33.244 --> 00:32:34.245
Wha...

383
00:32:36.456 --> 00:32:38.416
What would you
have me do. Mother?

384
00:32:40.418 --> 00:32:42.837
Do simply what is needed of you:

385
00:32:44.547 --> 00:32:45.965
nothing.

386
00:33:16.121 --> 00:33:17.539
On your feet!

387
00:33:19.416 --> 00:33:21.334
To Rook's Rest!

388
00:33:22.627 --> 00:33:24.045
To battle!

389
00:33:29.175 --> 00:33:31.093
It's broad daylight.

390
00:33:31.094 --> 00:33:34.555
We must hold here and ready
ourselves to lay siege at nightfall.

391
00:33:34.556 --> 00:33:37.933
We shall move now and strike by
day. They will not expect it.

392
00:33:37.934 --> 00:33:41.438
They will not expect it
because it is fucking madness.

393
00:33:43.773 --> 00:33:46.293
Did you forget the little encounter
we had on the road to Rosby?

394
00:33:47.027 --> 00:33:48.236
I did not.

395
00:33:50.155 --> 00:33:53.158
Dragonstone and their dragons
are just across the bay.

396
00:33:54.576 --> 00:33:56.578
What? Grown tired
of living. have you?

397
00:33:57.537 --> 00:33:59.080
Are you afraid. Ser?

398
00:34:00.165 --> 00:34:02.417
Worse. I'm rational.

399
00:34:04.544 --> 00:34:05.962
We advance.

400
00:34:26.566 --> 00:34:28.317
I see no other choice.

401
00:34:28.318 --> 00:34:30.695
- We need to send a dragon.
- Where?

402
00:34:36.076 --> 00:34:40.162
To support the war that your vassals
have been fighting in your absence.

403
00:34:40.163 --> 00:34:41.456
Your Grace.

404
00:34:42.749 --> 00:34:45.918
Cole's host has grown
since riding abroad.

405
00:34:45.919 --> 00:34:48.128
He raised the levies of
both Rosby and Stokeworth

406
00:34:48.129 --> 00:34:51.048
and. with their combined
strength. sacked Duskendale.

407
00:34:51.049 --> 00:34:52.675
Duskendale?

408
00:34:52.676 --> 00:34:54.718
The city has fallen.

409
00:34:54.719 --> 00:34:56.720
Many Darklyn men
declared for Aegon.

410
00:34:56.721 --> 00:34:58.597
Those who refused
were put to the sword.

411
00:34:58.598 --> 00:35:00.432
What of my father?

412
00:35:00.433 --> 00:35:01.851
He kept his oath.

413
00:35:02.435 --> 00:35:04.270
Cole took his head for it.

414
00:35:06.481 --> 00:35:09.149
Where have you been.
these last days?

415
00:35:09.150 --> 00:35:11.861
You vanished without
so much as a word.

416
00:35:12.612 --> 00:35:15.656
Well. I apologize for my
absence and the secrecy.

417
00:35:15.657 --> 00:35:17.742
but such was necessary.

418
00:35:18.576 --> 00:35:19.911
I went to King's Landing.

419
00:35:21.538 --> 00:35:23.163
To what possible end?

420
00:35:23.164 --> 00:35:25.541
To meet Queen Alicent
and sue for peace.

421
00:35:25.542 --> 00:35:28.293
- You saw Alicent?
- Yes. I did.

422
00:35:28.294 --> 00:35:30.671
You could've been
taken or slain!

423
00:35:30.672 --> 00:35:34.591
I inherited 80 years of
peace from my father.

424
00:35:34.592 --> 00:35:36.260
Before I was to end it.

425
00:35:36.261 --> 00:35:39.347
I needed to know that
there was no other path.

426
00:35:41.891 --> 00:35:43.518
And now I do.

427
00:35:47.105 --> 00:35:49.023
Only one choice remains to me:

428
00:35:49.024 --> 00:35:52.235
either I win my claim or die.

429
00:35:54.988 --> 00:35:57.240
We stand at the ready.

430
00:35:58.158 --> 00:36:00.367
Cole's victories have
only emboldened him.

431
00:36:00.368 --> 00:36:02.494
He marches on Rook's Rest.

432
00:36:02.495 --> 00:36:06.123
His host was just hours away when
Lord Staunton's ravens took wing.

433
00:36:06.124 --> 00:36:08.625
Why Rook's Rest?
After Duskendale?

434
00:36:08.626 --> 00:36:10.794
It is but a small coastal keep.

435
00:36:10.795 --> 00:36:14.548
'Cause Lord Staunton is
a member of this council.

436
00:36:14.549 --> 00:36:18.510
And because his castle is small and
vulnerable and there for the taking.

437
00:36:18.511 --> 00:36:20.971
Cole knows we have no
army on the mainland.

438
00:36:20.972 --> 00:36:23.515
- He is brazen.
- He is daring us to act.

439
00:36:23.516 --> 00:36:25.852
We need to send a dragon.

440
00:36:33.568 --> 00:36:37.113
There are those who have
mistaken my caution for weakness.

441
00:36:42.202 --> 00:36:44.204
Let that be their undoing.

442
00:36:45.080 --> 00:36:47.247
- I will go.
- My queen...

443
00:36:47.248 --> 00:36:50.125
- You cannot.
- I will not lose dragons to war

444
00:36:50.126 --> 00:36:51.502
whilst I hide here in my castle.

445
00:36:51.503 --> 00:36:54.672
Our allies raise their
banners for you. Mother.

446
00:36:54.673 --> 00:36:56.715
Yes. they do.

447
00:36:56.716 --> 00:36:59.843
If you die. all is lost.

448
00:36:59.844 --> 00:37:01.428
- Send me.
- No.

449
00:37:01.429 --> 00:37:03.430
I will burn Cole's lines and
withdraw before King's Landing

450
00:37:03.431 --> 00:37:05.631
- could even raise the alarm.
- You lack the experience.

451
00:37:08.395 --> 00:37:10.689
You must send me. Your Grace.

452
00:37:12.941 --> 00:37:16.403
Meleys is your largest dragon
and no stranger to battle.

453
00:37:19.197 --> 00:37:20.990
I will meet Cole.

454
00:38:29.642 --> 00:38:33.479
I wish only to fight for
you. for your claim and mine.

455
00:38:33.480 --> 00:38:35.023
I...

456
00:38:36.441 --> 00:38:38.121
There's something I
need to tell you. Jace.

457
00:38:40.653 --> 00:38:46.326
Something I should've told you when
you first became heir to the throne.

458
00:38:47.619 --> 00:38:52.707
<i>It's a secret that Viserys told
me when he named me his successor.</i>

459
00:38:53.708 --> 00:38:56.711
<i>And it has passed
from king to heir</i>

460
00:38:57.545 --> 00:39:00.382
<i>since Aegon the
Conqueror's time.</i>

461
00:39:08.682 --> 00:39:12.519
<i>I never told you because I was
unsure that I believed it myself.</i>

462
00:39:14.062 --> 00:39:17.856
<i>The Targaryen who
sits the Iron Throne</i>

463
00:39:17.857 --> 00:39:20.317
<i>is not just a king or a queen.</i>

464
00:39:20.318 --> 00:39:22.112
<i>They are a Protector.</i>

465
00:39:26.574 --> 00:39:30.120
<i>Ordained to lead the Seven
Kingdoms. to strengthen them.</i>

466
00:39:32.664 --> 00:39:36.668
<i>and to unite them
against a common foe.</i>

467
00:39:41.214 --> 00:39:44.426
<i>Viserys chose me to succeed him.</i>

468
00:39:45.468 --> 00:39:47.721
<i>He held to this the
whole of his life.</i>

469
00:39:53.727 --> 00:39:58.940
<i>My father believed that I. alone.
was meant to be this Protector.</i>

470
00:40:00.108 --> 00:40:03.069
They're 1.400-. 1.500-strong
at least. my lord.

471
00:40:04.654 --> 00:40:08.033
<i>But to unite the realm. I had
to send the dragons to war.</i>

472
00:40:16.875 --> 00:40:20.420
The horrors I have just loosed
cannot be for a crown alone.

473
00:40:22.630 --> 00:40:24.673
<i>That is why I must believe</i>

474
00:40:24.674 --> 00:40:27.801
<i>what Viserys told me when
he named me his heir.</i>

475
00:40:27.802 --> 00:40:30.096
<i>What Jaehaerys had told him.</i>

476
00:40:30.930 --> 00:40:33.224
<i>And what I will now tell you.</i>

477
00:40:36.019 --> 00:40:37.062
What is it?

478
00:40:43.443 --> 00:40:45.653
Aegon the Conqueror's Dream.

479
00:40:47.822 --> 00:40:51.451
He called it "The
Song of Ice and Fire."

480
00:41:01.211 --> 00:41:03.254
Loose! New rank!

481
00:41:04.464 --> 00:41:07.384
Loose! New rank!

482
00:41:08.551 --> 00:41:10.929
Loose! New rank!

483
00:41:15.642 --> 00:41:16.643
Push it!

484
00:41:17.811 --> 00:41:19.062
Dragon!

485
00:41:19.646 --> 00:41:21.231
Dragon!

486
00:41:25.777 --> 00:41:28.405
To the Seven Hells
with you. Cole!

487
00:41:28.863 --> 00:41:31.156
You may as well have sounded
horns to announce our coming!

488
00:41:31.157 --> 00:41:33.200
Order the Darklyn levies to
break off and move ahead.

489
00:41:33.201 --> 00:41:35.119
We must keep the dragon's
attention divided.

490
00:41:35.120 --> 00:41:37.121
- Make the signal.
- What signal?

491
00:41:37.122 --> 00:41:38.957
All is going to plan.

492
00:42:36.473 --> 00:42:37.473
{\an8}IDIOT.

493
00:42:39.601 --> 00:42:42.102
{\an8}WAIT. VHAGAR.

494
00:42:42.103 --> 00:42:44.981
{\an8}NOT YET.

495
00:43:11.216 --> 00:43:12.801
Forward. Sunfyre!

496
00:43:13.593 --> 00:43:15.095
Faster!

497
00:43:15.637 --> 00:43:17.638
Dragon!

498
00:43:17.639 --> 00:43:18.932
Whose dragon is that?

499
00:43:19.808 --> 00:43:21.434
His Grace. the king's.

500
00:43:22.560 --> 00:43:24.687
This was your secret plot. Cole?

501
00:43:24.688 --> 00:43:26.480
For the king himself
to lay ambush

502
00:43:26.481 --> 00:43:28.774
- and mayhaps die in the attempt?
- No!

503
00:43:28.775 --> 00:43:30.694
Loose more signal arrows!

504
00:43:34.322 --> 00:43:36.324
Stalwart men of House Targaryen.

505
00:43:37.659 --> 00:43:40.078
your king has joined you!

506
00:43:41.037 --> 00:43:43.789
Hold to your courage!
Hold to your wits!

507
00:43:43.790 --> 00:43:49.003
For the Seven have blessed and
shielded this host with divine purpose!

508
00:43:49.004 --> 00:43:51.922
For the one true king. Aegon!

509
00:43:51.923 --> 00:43:54.551
Advance!

510
00:44:02.767 --> 00:44:04.769
Where are you. Aemond?

511
00:44:16.656 --> 00:44:18.700
{\an8}ATTACK. MELEYS!

512
00:44:19.909 --> 00:44:21.327
<i>Dracarys!</i>

513
00:45:00.408 --> 00:45:02.368
Another one there!

514
00:45:02.369 --> 00:45:04.661
Send a volley to
those Rosby men!

515
00:45:04.662 --> 00:45:06.748
Give them no quarter!

516
00:45:16.132 --> 00:45:18.134
We'd best get you
to cover. my lord.

517
00:46:06.766 --> 00:46:08.685
Thank the gods!

518
00:46:10.270 --> 00:46:11.438
<i>Dracarys!</i>

519
00:46:17.027 --> 00:46:19.070
No! No!

520
00:46:38.506 --> 00:46:39.924
Your Grace!

521
00:46:56.775 --> 00:46:58.693
{\an8}ATTACK. MELEYS.

522
00:51:46.523 --> 00:51:48.733
Fall in behind me!

523
00:51:49.693 --> 00:51:51.653
Into the breach!

524
00:52:23.226 --> 00:52:25.729
The king has fallen.
We must find him.

525
00:53:15.862 --> 00:53:17.238
Aemond!

526
00:53:32.629 --> 00:53:34.172
Where's His Grace?

527
00:53:35.305 --> 00:54:35.801
